        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephan Lichtsteiner, Winston Groom\n- Works: Forrest Gump\n- Roles: right-back, wing-back\n- Concepts: nicknames, playing style\n\nFacts:\n- In 1986, Winston Groom published the novel Forrest Gump.\n- In 1994, Forrest Gump was released as an American comedy-drama film based on Winston Groom's 1986 novel of the same name.\n- Stephan Lichtsteiner played as an attacking right-back or wing-back.\n- Stephan Lichtsteiner was known for energetic runs down the right wing, stamina, and athleticism.\n- Stephan Lichtsteiner's stamina and athleticism earned him the nicknames \"Forrest Gump\" and \"The Swiss Express\".",
